{"nbformat":4,"nbformat_minor":5,"metadata":{"colab":{"provenance":[]},"kernelspec":{"name":"python3","display_name":"Python 3"},"language_info":{"name":"python"}},"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["# Phase VI — Head-to-head: Tarozo ordinal patterns vs multiscale level-set geometry\n","\n","This version is prepared for the **private** `ardominguezm/painting-geometry` repository.\n","\n","The shell inside Colab is not automatically authenticated just because the notebook was opened from GitHub. The first cell therefore uses a GitHub Personal Access Token (PAT) securely through `GIT_ASKPASS`; the token is never placed in the clone URL or printed.\n","\n","Primary question:\n","\n","\\[\n","\\boxed{\\text{Does multiscale level-set curvature add information beyond tie-aware ordinal patterns?}}\n","\\]\n","\n","The comparison uses the same ArtBench pilot and the same artist-disjoint nested-CV protocol as Phase IV/IVb."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["import os, sys, subprocess, shutil, getpass\n","from pathlib import Path\n","\n","REPO_URL = \"https://github.com/ardominguezm/painting-geometry.git\"\n","BRANCH = \"multiscale-corpus-analysis\"\n","REPO_DIR = Path(\"/content/painting-geometry\")\n","\n","os.chdir(\"/content\")\n","if REPO_DIR.exists():\n","    shutil.rmtree(REPO_DIR)\n","\n","# Prefer a Colab Secret named GITHUB_TOKEN; otherwise prompt without echo.\n","token = None\n","try:\n","    from google.colab import userdata\n","    token = userdata.get(\"GITHUB_TOKEN\")\n","except Exception:\n","    pass\n","\n","if not token:\n","    token = getpass.getpass(\n","        \"GitHub PAT for the private painting-geometry repo \"\n","        \"(fine-grained token with Contents: Read-only): \"\n","    )\n","\n","askpass = Path(\"/tmp/github_askpass.sh\")\n","askpass.write_text(\n","    '#!/bin/sh\\n'\n","    'case \"$1\" in\\n'\n","    '  *Username*) echo \"x-access-token\" ;;\\n'\n","    '  *Password*) echo \"$GITHUB_TOKEN\" ;;\\n'\n","    'esac\\n'\n",")\n","askpass.chmod(0o700)\n","\n","env = os.environ.copy()\n","env[\"GIT_ASKPASS\"] = str(askpass)\n","env[\"GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT\"] = \"0\"\n","env[\"GITHUB_TOKEN\"] = token\n","\n","try:\n","    subprocess.run(\n","        [\"git\", \"clone\", \"--depth\", \"1\", \"--branch\", BRANCH, \"--single-branch\",\n","         REPO_URL, str(REPO_DIR)],\n","        check=True, env=env\n","    )\n","finally:\n","    askpass.unlink(missing_ok=True)\n","    env.pop(\"GITHUB_TOKEN\", None)\n","    token = None\n","\n","subprocess.run(\n","    [sys.executable, \"-m\", \"pip\", \"install\", \"-q\", \"-r\", str(REPO_DIR/\"requirements.txt\")],\n","    check=True\n",")\n","subprocess.run(\n","    [sys.executable, \"-m\", \"pip\", \"install\", \"-q\", \"ordpy>=1.2.0\"],\n","    check=True\n",")\n","\n","os.chdir(REPO_DIR)\n","if str(REPO_DIR) not in sys.path:\n","    sys.path.insert(0, str(REPO_DIR))\n","\n","import numpy as np, pandas as pd, ordpy\n","print(\"Branch:\", BRANCH)\n","print(\"Commit:\", subprocess.check_output([\"git\",\"rev-parse\",\"HEAD\"], text=True).strip())\n","print(\"ordpy:\", getattr(ordpy, \"__version__\", \"unknown\"))\n","assert hasattr(ordpy, \"two_by_two_patterns\")\n","print(\"Setup OK\")"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## Upload previous outputs\n","\n","Upload both ZIP files:\n","\n","- `painting_geometry_phase4_artbench_pilot.zip`\n","- `painting_geometry_phase4b_scale_hierarchy.zip`"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["from google.colab import files\n","import zipfile\n","\n","uploaded = files.upload()\n","names = list(uploaded)\n","print(\"Uploaded:\", names)\n","\n","phase4_name = next((n for n in names if \"phase4_artbench_pilot\" in n), None)\n","phase4b_name = next((n for n in names if \"phase4b_scale_hierarchy\" in n), None)\n","if not phase4_name or not phase4b_name:\n","    raise FileNotFoundError(\"Upload both Phase IV and Phase IVb ZIP files.\")\n","\n","INPUT_DIR = Path(\"/content/phase6_inputs\")\n","if INPUT_DIR.exists():\n","    shutil.rmtree(INPUT_DIR)\n","INPUT_DIR.mkdir()\n","\n","for n in [phase4_name, phase4b_name]:\n","    with zipfile.ZipFile(Path(\"/content\")/n) as z:\n","        z.extractall(INPUT_DIR)\n","\n","def one(pattern):\n","    hits = list(INPUT_DIR.rglob(pattern))\n","    if not hits:\n","        raise FileNotFoundError(pattern)\n","    print(pattern, \"->\", hits[0])\n","    return hits[0]\n","\n","FEATURES = one(\"artbench_pilot_features.csv\")\n","ALL_OOF = one(\"artbench10_all_phase4b_oof_predictions.csv\")\n","W8_OOF = one(\"artbench10_wikiart8_phase4b_oof_predictions.csv\")\n","\n","feat = pd.read_csv(FEATURES)\n","print(\"Pilot matrix:\", feat.shape)\n","display(feat[[\"split\",\"style\",\"artist\",\"filename\"]].head())"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## Download ArtBench-10 256×256 images\n","\n","Ordinal patterns must be extracted from the actual paintings. This cell downloads the 256×256 ImageFolder split only."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["import tarfile\n","import kagglehub\n","\n","DATA_DIR = Path(\"/content/artbench_data\")\n","DATA_DIR.mkdir(exist_ok=True)\n","TAR_NAME = \"artbench-10-imagefolder-split.tar\"\n","KAGGLE_HANDLE = \"alexanderliao/artbench10\"\n","\n","tar_path = None\n","for candidate in [\n","    TAR_NAME,\n","    f\"256X256/{TAR_NAME}\",\n","    f\"data/256X256/{TAR_NAME}\",\n","    f\"ArtBench-10/data/256X256/{TAR_NAME}\",\n","]:\n","    try:\n","        print(\"Trying Kaggle:\", candidate)\n","        p = Path(kagglehub.dataset_download(KAGGLE_HANDLE, path=candidate))\n","        if p.exists():\n","            tar_path = p\n","            print(\"Found:\", p)\n","            break\n","    except Exception as exc:\n","        print(\"  not found:\", type(exc).__name__)\n","\n","if tar_path is None:\n","    raise RuntimeError(\n","        \"Could not obtain the ArtBench 256 split from Kaggle. \"\n","        \"Check Kaggle connectivity and rerun this cell.\"\n","    )\n","\n","EXTRACT_DIR = DATA_DIR/\"imagefolder\"\n","EXTRACT_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n","print(\"Extracting:\", tar_path)\n","with tarfile.open(tar_path) as tf:\n","    try:\n","        tf.extractall(EXTRACT_DIR, filter=\"data\")\n","    except TypeError:\n","        tf.extractall(EXTRACT_DIR)\n","\n","train_dirs = list(EXTRACT_DIR.rglob(\"train\"))\n","print(\"Candidate train dirs:\", train_dirs[:5])\n","if not train_dirs:\n","    raise RuntimeError(\"ArtBench extraction did not produce a train directory.\")"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## Extract Tarozo et al. ordinal representations\n","\n","For every pilot image this computes:\n","- 75 tie-aware two-by-two ordinal probabilities;\n","- 11 grouped pattern probabilities;\n","- 24 standard ordinal probabilities;\n","- the \\(H,C\\) complexity–entropy pair."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["RESULTS = REPO_DIR/\"results\"/\"phase6_ordinal_head_to_head\"\n","RESULTS.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n","ENRICHED = RESULTS/\"artbench_pilot_features_with_ordinals.csv\"\n","\n","subprocess.run([\n","    sys.executable, \"-u\", \"scripts/extract_tarozo_ordinal_features.py\",\n","    \"--features\", str(FEATURES),\n","    \"--dataset-root\", str(EXTRACT_DIR),\n","    \"--output\", str(ENRICHED),\n","    \"--checkpoint-every\", \"250\",\n","] , check=True)\n","\n","enriched = pd.read_csv(ENRICHED)\n","print(\"Enriched:\", enriched.shape)\n","print(\"OP75:\", sum(c.startswith(\"ord75__\") for c in enriched))\n","print(\"OP11:\", sum(c.startswith(\"ord11__\") for c in enriched))\n","print(\"OP24:\", sum(c.startswith(\"ord24__\") for c in enriched))\n","print(\"HC:\", sum(c.startswith(\"ordhc__\") for c in enriched))\n","display(enriched[[c for c in enriched.columns if c.startswith(\"ordmeta__\")]].describe().T)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## Artist-disjoint head-to-head\n","\n","All representations use identical outer artist-disjoint folds and training-only hyperparameter selection."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["EXP_DIR = RESULTS/\"experiments\"\n","EXP_DIR.mkdir(exist_ok=True)\n","\n","subprocess.run([\n","    sys.executable, \"-u\", \"scripts/run_ordinal_geometry_head_to_head.py\",\n","    \"--features\", str(ENRICHED),\n","    \"--output-dir\", str(EXP_DIR),\n","    \"--phase4b-all-oof\", str(ALL_OOF),\n","    \"--phase4b-wiki8-oof\", str(W8_OOF),\n","    \"--outer-folds\", \"5\",\n","    \"--inner-folds\", \"3\",\n","    \"--n-jobs\", \"-1\",\n","    \"--metric-boot\", \"2000\",\n","    \"--delta-boot\", \"5000\",\n"], check=True)\n","\n","R = pd.read_csv(EXP_DIR/\"phase6_head_to_head_results.csv\")\n","D = pd.read_csv(EXP_DIR/\"phase6_head_to_head_deltas.csv\")\n","\n","print(\"\\nRESULTS\")\n","display(R.sort_values([\"dataset\",\"macro_f1_oof\"], ascending=[True,False]))\n","print(\"\\nDELTAS\")\n","display(D)"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## Export\n","\n","Download the complete Phase VI output ZIP and upload it back to ChatGPT for interpretation."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["import shutil\n","zip_base = Path(\"/content/painting_geometry_phase6_ordinal_head_to_head\")\n","zip_path = shutil.make_archive(str(zip_base), \"zip\", root_dir=RESULTS)\n","print(\"ZIP:\", zip_path)\n","files.download(zip_path)"]}]}